  "body": "### Description\r\nThis ticket is to introduce the support in OONI for HTTPS security measurement following the  M-15-13 requirements implemented also by the tools PSHTT (https://github.com/dhs-ncats/pshtt) that's also the basis of the Secure The News HTTPS/Media monitoring platform (https://github.com/freedomofpress/securethenews) .\r\n\r\nHaving an OONIProbe module that does the measurement of HTTPS security it would be possible to engage in massive monitoring of existing website lists (ex: all the media of a country or all the hospital of a country or all the government website of a country) to check:\r\n- If they are secure from the HTTPS measurement matrix above\r\n- If they do block users coming from Tor\r\n\r\nWith the ability to do that kind of monitoring \"in scale\" (also on Alexa Top 1 million or on very big lists), then it would be nice to evaluate which data analysis and visualization tools exists for OONI that could be leverage/partially re-purposed for that scope.\r\n\r\nThe general concept behind that feature is to leverage the existing structured OONI framework to do that kind of civic activism monitoring actions.",
